1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,940
克拉克森：今晚有几个重磅挑战：
你能拿汽车当飞镖玩吗？
CLARKSON: Tonight, some big challenges:
can you play darts with cars?

2
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:11,740
福特和鸽子，
究竟哪个更快？
Which is faster?
A Ford or a pigeon?

3
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:15,300
还有，这台全新的保时捷
能否在我们赛道上
刷新圈速纪录？
And can this new Porsche
break the lap record
on our track?

4
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,580
大家晚上好，
欢迎来到这台奥迪A8。
Good evening
and welcome to the Audi A8.

5
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:27,420
眼前这台车搭载的，
是一台双涡轮增压的
V8柴油发动机。
Now, this one has
a twin turbo-charged,
V8 diesel engine.

6
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:31,300
它零到六十英里加速
只要六秒，
相当给力。
It does naught to 60
in six seconds
and that's brilliant.

7
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:36,780
但按常理来说，买柴油车
图的不就是省油嘛。
But surely, the whole point
of a diesel engine
is fuel economy.

8
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:38,900
所以，我打算给自己
找点挑战。
So, I thought I'd set myself
a bit of a challenge.

9
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:44,580
看看我能不能开着这台大块头，
从伦敦一路开到爱丁堡，
See if I could drive this
enormous car
from London to Edinburgh

10
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:45,700
只用单单这一箱油。
on a single tank of fuel.

11
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,340
现在，谁觉得这行得通？
Now, who thinks
that's possible?

12
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,900
观众：不可能！
AUDIENCE: No.

13
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,980
你觉得行？不行？
有人觉得能成吗？
You think it's possible. No?
Anyone think it is possible?

14
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:54,380
你觉得能成？
You think it is possible?

15
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,340
-男观众：绝对没问题。
-绝对没问题？
-MAN: Definitely possible.
-Definitely possible?

16
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:59,620
可问题是，我自己的车
加满油也就跑270英里，对吧？
See, the thing is, my car
does 270 miles
before it's out. Yeah?

17
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:02,820
我妈还天天跟我念叨，
说她那辆小本田飞度
一箱油能跑340英里呢。
My mum's forever telling me
that her little Honda Jazz
does 340 miles.

18
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:06,020
你们觉得我开这玩意能跑400英里？
You think I could do
400 miles in that?

19
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:07,660
行吧，那要是我再加点码呢？
All right,
what if I up the ante a bit?

20
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:11,620
要是我……要是我试着
从伦敦开到爱丁堡，
What if... What if I tried to
drive from London to Edinburgh

21
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:15,100
然后再开回伦敦，
全程只靠这一箱油呢？
and then back to London again
on a single tank?

22
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:16,580
-不行？
-观众：不行！
-No?
-AUDIENCE: No.

23
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:18,100
-你们觉得没戏？
-绝不可能。[笑声]
-You don't think so?
-No. [LAUGHS]

24
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:21,140
好吧。反正你们才是专家。
呃，算半个专家吧。
Right. Well,
you're the experts.
Well, sort of.

25
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:23,420
-多谢了。
这么说，来回整整800英里？
-没错。
-Thank you.
So, that's 800 miles?
-Yeah.

26
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,580
-开这台车，V8双涡轮……
-对啊。
-In this car, V8 twin turbo...
-Yeah.

27
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:27,780
-不做任何改装，就一箱油？
-没门儿。
-No modifications,
one tank of fuel?
-Nope.

28
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:29,980
-这主意蠢透了。
-确实蠢。
-That's a stupid idea.
-Yeah.

29
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:33,660
你疯了吧。除非你把整个后备箱
全灌满柴油，
否则你绝对搞不定。
You're mad. Unless you fill
the whole boot with diesel,
you're not gonna do it.

30
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:34,940
我也深表赞同。
I agreed with that.

31
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:37,580
但现在油价都涨到……多少来着？4块……
But fuel's now running out
at what? 4...

32
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:39,780
-两人合：4镑50。
-每加仑大概4镑50。
-BOTH: £4.50.
-About £4.50 a gallon.

33
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:45,180
所以现在正是时候，
看看一加仑油到底能
被压榨出多少英里来。
So probably a good time now
to see just how many miles
you can eke from a gallon.

34
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,780
因此，我欣然接受了
自己的这项挑战。
I therefore accepted
my own challenge.

35
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:50,340
[模仿美式口音]
我是杰克·鲍尔。
[IN AMERICAN ACCENT]
My name is Jack Bauer.

36
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:53,100
而这将是我人生中
最省油的24小时。
And this is the most
economical 24 hours
of my life.

37
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:54,260
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

38
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,340
[紧张的背景音乐响起]
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

39
00:01:57,380 --> 00:02:01,780
现在是早上七点整，
出发正当时，
It's 7:00 a.m. and this is
a good time to start,

40
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:03,980
一方面是因为
此时路上清静不堵
partly because
the roads are quiet

41
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:08,460
还有一部分原因在于，
现在正是加油的绝佳时机。
and partly because
this is a good time
for filling up with fuel.

42
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:15,740
你们看，在大清早，
天气还很冷的时候——今早确实冷得要命——
You see, in the morning,
when it's cold, and it is
very cold this morning,

43
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:21,100
燃油的密度会比
炎热的下午更高，
fuel is more dense than it is
on a hot afternoon,

44
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:24,580
所以花同样的钱，
你能加到更多油。
so you're getting
a little bit more
for your money.

45
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,500
不过还有一点。
One thing, though.

46
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:33,300
无论如何，千万别忘了
把后备箱里所有没用的累赘
统统清理出去。
Don't, whatever you do,
forget to take any unnecessary
weight out of the boot.

47
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:48,020
好了，油箱里灌了19.8加仑油，
前方是一段整整800英里的漫长旅程。
Right, I've got 19.8 gallons
in the tank and a journey of
800 miles ahead of me.

48
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:51,900
这意味着平均油耗必须达到
每加仑40.4英里。
That means averaging
40.4 miles to the gallon.

49
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:58,740
对于一辆马力如此强悍的车来说，
简直是强人所难。
A tall order in a car
as powerful as this.

50
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:02,140
就连奥迪官方都说，
我想干的事根本就不可能。
Even Audi say that what
I'm attempting to do
is impossible.

51
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:05,900
他们说这车顶多只能跑出
每加仑37英里，
They say this car will only do
37 miles to the gallon

52
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:07,940
我绝对撑不到回程。
and that I won't make it back.

53
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,860
不过，我还是有一两招
能帮上点忙的。
There are one or two things
I can do to help, though.

54
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:20,940
你必须确保车身切开空气时
阻力尽可能小。
You have to make sure
the car cuts as smooth a hole
as possible in the air.

55
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:26,820
举个例子，开着车窗跑，
油耗就会暴增5%。
Driving with the window down,
for instance, increases
fuel consumption by 5%.

56
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:28,460
更糟糕的是，
And to make matters worse,

57
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,980
你连空调也不能开，
you can't use
the air conditioning either

58
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,460
因为那玩意儿对油耗的杀伤力更大。
because that does
even more damage.

59
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:36,780
就拿一辆本田思域来说吧，
In a Honda Civic,
for instance,

60
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:38,980
如果平时正常能跑每加仑36英里，
if you get 36 miles
to the gallon normally,

61
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:42,540
你只要把空调一开，
立刻暴跌到
每加仑30英里。
you turn the air-con on,
that drops to
30 miles to the gallon.

62
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:46,500
平白无故损失6 MPG。
You lose 6 MPG.

63
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:51,420
事实上，除非人命关天，
车里的任何电器设备都碰不得。
In fact, you shouldn't use
any electrical gadgets unless
it's absolutely necessary.

64
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:54,180
后车窗加热绝对想都别想。
The heated rear window's
a complete no-no.

65
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:57,060
至于座椅加热？趁早死心吧。
And heated seats, forget it.

66
00:03:57,100 --> 00:04:02,380
万幸的是，收音机耗电极小，
这个我总算还能听听。
Happily, the radio uses such
a small amount of power
that I can use that.

67
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:06,740
但调查研究表明，
节奏快、暴躁的音乐
But surveys have shown
that fast, aggressive music

68
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,060
-会让司机忍不住狂轰油门。
-[重金属音乐响起]
-causes drivers
to grow lead feet.
-[METAL MUSIC PLAYING]

69
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:14,860
所以激流金属乐不仅震碎你的耳膜，
还会掏空你的钱包。
So, thrash metal doesn't just
hurt your ears, it
damages your wallet as well.

70
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,740
[音乐停止]
[MUSIC STOPS]

71
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:19,660
那这一路，
只能全程锁定BBC广播二台了。
On this journey,
then, it will be
Radio 2 all the way.

72
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:22,100
[欢快音乐响起]
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:26,340
电台DJ：那么，这首歌是在90年代的哪一年再次爆红的呢？
是95年、97年还是99年？
RADIO DJ: So, was that a hit
again in the 90's in '95,
'97 or '99?

74
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:27,940
97年。
'97.

75
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:30,260
电台女听众：
我不知道，
我觉得是95年。
WOMAN ON RADIO:
I don't know.
I think '95.

76
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,980
-电台DJ：不对，是97年……
-瞧见没？
-RADIO DJ: No, it was '97...
-You see?

77
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:34,100
运气真背……来自Sad Café乐队。
Bad luck...Sad Cafe.

78
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:36,740
克拉克森：我发现了一件挺有意思的事，
刚出发的时候，
CLARKSON: There's one
interesting thing I've noticed
that when I started out,

79
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:38,260
我开着定速巡航，
当时的平均油耗——
I had the cruise control on
and I was averaging,

80
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,460
根据行车电脑显示——
according to
the trip computer,

81
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,580
差不多32、33
英里每加仑。
about 32, 33
miles to the gallon.

82
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:45,500
自从我关掉定速巡航，
改用自己的右脚控制之后，
Since I've taken
the cruise control off
and I'm using my own foot,

83
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:48,980
我已经把平均油耗提到了
40英里每加仑，
I've got it up to an average
of 40 miles to the gallon,

84
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,860
差不多快达到目标了。
which is nearly good enough.

85
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:54,180
不可思议的是，
你得费多少脑子、精神得有多集中，
It's amazing how much
thinking and concentrating
you have to do

86
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:55,580
才能开得这么省油。
to drive economically.

87
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:57,220
你得琢磨：“前面那哥们儿要停吗？
You got to think
"Is that guy gonna pull up?

88
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:59,700
我得配合他的车速。收油门……”
"I've got to match my speed
to him. Lifting off..."

89
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:01,300
你绝对、绝对不能踩刹车。
You must never ever brake.

90
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:04,140
千千万万别碰刹车。
碰都别碰。
Ever, ever touch the brakes.
Ever.

91
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:07,900
要是平时大家飙车时
也能这么全神贯注，
If people concentrated
this hard to drive fast,

92
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:10,180
世界上就绝对不会有车祸了。绝对没有。
no one would ever crash. Ever.

93
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,500
[滴答声]
[TICKING]

94
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:20,900
啊，这里是东北部，
到处是连绵起伏的山丘，
Ah, this is the northeast
where there are many hills,

95
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:24,700
而山坡对一个
一心想省油的司机来说，
简直是天大的麻烦。
and hills are
a big problem for the
economy-minded motorist.

96
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:29,980
诀窍是在遇到斜坡前
先把速度冲上去，
The trick is to build up speed
before you get to an incline

97
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:33,020
等上了坡，
就尽量不要再踩油门加速。
and then try not to accelerate
when you're on it.

98
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:35,020
[重金属乐响起]
[METAL MUSIC PLAYING]

99
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:37,740
所以，冲下坡时听敲击金属……
So, thrash metal
for going down a hill...

100
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,660
[舒缓音乐响起]
[SOOTHING MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:42,700
……爬上另一头时，就听卡朋特乐队。
...and then, the Carpenters
for going up the other side.

102
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,900
冲到坡顶，收油。
Reach the crest and off.

103
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:49,620
结果油耗居然才跑出
39英里每加仑！
And I've still only done
39 miles to the gallon!

104
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:52,260
你们到底还想要我怎样？！
What more do you want from me?

105
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:55,260
[凯尔特风音乐响起]
[CELTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

106
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,660
已经在路上开了整整六个小时。
Six hours on the road.

107
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:03,460
我觉得我真得撒泡尿了。
I think I do want a wee.

108
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:06,460
但我不能停，
因为停车就意味着得重新打火，
But I can't stop
because that would mean
starting the engine again,

109
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,580
而启动发动机
那可是极其费油的。
and starting an engine
uses a load of fuel.

110
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:12,140
所以，该用纽约出租车司机的绝招了——
So, a New York
taxi driver trick

111
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,980
你们不许偷看。
and you're
not allowed to watch.

112
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:21,380
要是我开的是汽油版的奥迪A8来爱丁堡，
Now, if I'd come to Edinburgh
in a petrol-powered Audi A8,

113
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:23,420
现在就得四处找加油站了。
I'd need to find
a filling station.

114
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:27,500
但多亏了
这辆车里的柴油发动机，
我根本用不着。
But thanks to
the diesel engine
in this one, I don't.

115
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:32,060
不过问题是，
The thing is, though,

116
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:35,100
车子不需要喝油，
我可渴得想喝上一杯了。
it might not need
a drink but I do.

117
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:37,260
所以，我想找个地方住下，
So, I think I'll find
somewhere to stay

118
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:40,380
明天早上咱们再接着搞。
and we'll pick this up again
in the morning.

119
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,780
[锁车声]
[CAR LOCKS]

120
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:53,380
我想，是时候汇报一下当前战况了，
但情况可不太妙。
Time, I think,
for a status report
and the news isn't good.

121
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:56,660
我们知道回伦敦
还有400英里。
We know it to be 400 miles
back to London.

122
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:59,060
再看看行车电脑，
And if we look
at the trip computer,

123
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:04,940
它显示我还有340英里
柴油就会耗尽。
[轻笑]
it tells me that I will
run out of diesel
[CHUCKLES] in 340 miles.

124
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:08,060
不过老式的传统油表
还能给我点心理安慰，
I can take some comfort from
the good, old-fashioned
fuel gauge,

125
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:09,940
上面显示我还有半箱油。
which says I have half a tank.

126
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:14,220
很好，来的时候用了半箱，
那么回程也就是半箱。
Good. Half a tank to get here,
therefore, half a tank
to get back.

127
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:17,060
但问题是，我来这儿用的可不止半箱。
Except I didn't use
half a tank getting here.

128
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,140
我用了半箱，
I used half a tank,

129
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:23,300
再加上加油颈管里多灌的那点油，
plus the amount that was in
the fuel filler pipe thing,

130
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:26,380
那大概有半加仑，
相当于23英里的里程。
and that was,
probably, half a gallon,
that's 23 miles.

131
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:30,980
而这23英里，回程我可没有了。
23 miles that I don't have
on the return leg.

132
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:35,140
我觉得我八成要抛锚在应急车道上了。
I think I'm going to wind up
on a hard shoulder.

133
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:41,180
行吧，待会儿咱们就能见分晓，
看我是能顺利开回去，
Well, we'll find out later on,
whether I make it back

134
